,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus","html_url":"https://github.com/jthegedus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jthegedus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-05-19T02:27:47Z","updated_at":"2021-05-19T03:11:44Z","body":"This was introduced in https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/pull/834\r\n\r\nGiven `--host` was implemented before `--https` my suggestion would be:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n    -p, --port     Port  (default 3000)\r\n-   -h, --host     Host (only use this on trusted networks)  (default localhost)\r\n+   -H, --host     Host (only use this on trusted networks)  (default localhost)\r\n-   -H, --https    Use self-signed HTTPS certificate  (default false)\r\n+   -S, --https    Use self-signed HTTPS certificate  (default false)\r\n\r\n    -o, --open     Open a browser tab  (default false)\r\n    -h, --help     Displays this message\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis aligns with [Sade docs](https://github.com/lukeed/sade#single-command-mode) which has examples with `-H, --host`, which likely informs first-time users and thus it is likely `-H` is used with `--host` elsewhere.\r\n\r\nNoteably, Vite doesn't have aliases for it's `--host` or `--https` options, likely because of this conflict.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/kit/issues/comments/843695939/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,